# =============================================================================
# CIMS — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. NEVER commit `.env`.
# Only variables prefixed `VITE_` are exposed to the browser bundle; everything
# else is server-side only (Edge Functions / CI) per docs/13_SECURITY_AND_PRIVACY.md.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — client (safe to expose; RLS is what protects the data)
#
# Local stack defaults printed by `supabase start`, which uses legacy
# anon/service_role JWTs. Newer hosted projects issue the `sb_publishable_...`
# / `sb_secret_...` key format instead — src/lib/supabase.ts and Edge
# Functions accept either naming, preferring the PUBLISHABLE_KEY/SECRET_KEY
# form when both are set. Use whichever pair your target project issues.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

VITE_APP_ENV=development

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — server only. NEVER prefix these with VITE_.
# The service-role/secret key bypasses RLS entirely. It belongs in Edge
# Function secrets and CI, never in the browser.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=
SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploying the schema to a hosted (non-local) project.
#
# `supabase link --project-ref <ref>` and `supabase db push` need ONE of the
# two credentials below — neither is a project API key, and neither should
# ever go in this file even as a real value in a real .env; both are
# account/infra-level secrets, not application config:
#   - SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN   a personal access token from
#     https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
#   - the project's direct Postgres password, to build SUPABASE_DB_URL as
#     postgresql://postgres:<password>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# Until one of those is supplied for a given hosted project, that project's
# database has none of this repo's migrations applied, regardless of which
# API keys are configured above.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KAREN — AI provider (server side only, Edge Functions: supabase/functions/karen-chat)
#
# These are NOT read from this .env file at runtime — the Edge Function reads
# its own secrets, set via `supabase secrets set KAREN_PROVIDER=... --project-ref <ref>`
# (or the Dashboard's Edge Functions > Secrets page), never from the frontend
# build. This file documents the values to set, and is what `supabase
# functions serve --env-file supabase/functions/.env` reads for local dev
# (copy this block into supabase/functions/.env, gitignored, for that).
#
# Setting KAREN_PROVIDER=gemini activates production inference against the
# real Gemini API (supabase/functions/karen-chat/providers/gemini.ts). A real
# key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey normally starts with "AIza" —
# if `KAREN_API_KEY` doesn't look like that, karen-chat will still run but
# every turn will fail with a PROVIDER_REQUEST_FAILED error until the key is
# corrected. Leaving KAREN_PROVIDER=fixture returns a typed
# PROVIDER_NOT_CONFIGURED-adjacent deterministic reply instead of a
# fabricated one (docs/22 ADR-004).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One of: fixture | gemini
KAREN_PROVIDER=fixture
KAREN_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash
KAREN_API_KEY=
KAREN_MAX_TOKENS=4096
KAREN_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# Per-user rate limiting for the KAREN conversation API (docs/44) — enforced
# by public.karen_check_rate_limit(), called from karen-chat/index.ts.
KAREN_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=20

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Geospatial
#
# BLOCKER: the real campus polygon and classroom coordinates are not available.
# No boundary is hard-coded anywhere in production logic. Campus geofences and
# classroom coordinates are configured at runtime through the application by an
# authorised user. Test fixtures use clearly-marked synthetic coordinates.
#
# Default classroom radius, metres (docs/05_GEOFENCING_SPEC.md).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CIMS_DEFAULT_CLASSROOM_RADIUS_M=20

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test-only credentials for the local stack. Not used in production.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TEST_USER_PASSWORD=
